Algorithm: Threaded Binary Tree Traversal
Start.
Create an empty Threaded Binary Search Tree.
Insert nodes into the tree while maintaining threads.
Set the current pointer to the root node.
Move to the leftmost node of the tree.
Display the current node's data.
If the right pointer is a thread, move to the inorder successor.
Otherwise, move to the right child and then find its leftmost node.
Repeat Steps 6–8 until the current pointer becomes NULL.
Stop.
